            </profile>
            <profile id="b24b-fce6-73eb-69da" name="Equipment and options (as printed in WAB2 army list)" publicationId="fcb9-17be-94c2-bcfc" hidden="false" typeId="b19e-ee0c-17d1-6e33" typeName="Equipment and Notes">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="63ac-8f60-d28a-2232">The Standard bearer rides a warhorse and has a hand weapon, heavy or partial plate armour and shield. Army Standard Bearer. May have cloth barding (+3). In an Early army, the Carrocio may replace the Army Standard. It is a War Wagon and follows all rules for War Wagons and counts as the Army Standard. The crew does not have War Wagon missile weapons, and the range of the effects of the Army Standard is 18’’ rather than 12’’.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
            <profile id="605b-4868-c046-ec45" name="Armour Save" hidden="false" typeId="0dbe-f4ed-ef08-8e86" typeName="Armour Save">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Save" typeId="603e-2898-6af9-6cf1">3+</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="With conditional bonuses" typeId="5882-dd5a-bc28-4024">-</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Notes" typeId="d5e4-804e-6192-0114">Armour save from armour, shield and barding bonus pips (rulebook pp.95-98); maximum 3+ (2+ for barded cavalry). M already includes encumbrance for armour/barding (p.96). Conditional pips are in the next column.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
              <!-- armour-save -->
            </profile>
          </profiles>
